{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MGindKMWWs8zsgiLW9uNyT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-538\"\n3\ttitle = \"Arm the complexity sensor here at the ruled scope, and re-base the module-size ratchet to SLOC (OI-68 phase 2, 1c)\"\n4\tspecref = \"\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = [\"WI-537\", \"~WI-521\"]\n8\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Deliverable\n14\t\n15\tExecuted OI-68 phase 2 at the ruled shape **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a** — arm + re-base,\n16\tnever arm + retire. Both sensors stay armed on different axes; nothing was deleted\n17\tand no pointer moved.\n18\t\n19\t1. **Armed (3a).** New `[step:complexity]` in `docs/stack.ini`\n20\t   (`command = {py} project-trajectory/scripts/check_complexity.py --root . --mode\n21\t   enforce`, `layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) — the exact-equality\n22\t   compare against `docs/complexity-baseline` in both directions, nonzero on\n23\t   either. Minted no spine row: `SR-183` already carries both postures (\"gated only\n24\t   where a repo opts in\"), and the opt-in is the step's presence here.\n25\t   `check_complexity.py`'s module docstring updated from \"report-only as shipped\" to\n26\t   \"report-only where shipped, armed here\". Shipped default stays report-only\n27\t   (that's phase 3, a separate WI).\n28\t\n29\t2. **Scoped (2a).** `check_complexity.DEFAULT_INCLUDE` widened to census `tests/`\n30\t   as well as `project-trajectory/scripts/`; `docs/complexity-baseline` re-stamped\n31\t   to seed the 20 `tests/` functions over threshold 15 (census now 200 rows: 180\n32\t   scripts + 20 tests). This closes WI-521 §3's sensor gap on the complexity axis;\n33\t   WI-521 amended in place to record that, and to state honestly what is still\n34\t   unwatched (test-tree *size* growth — no function crossing cognitive 15 — is\n35\t   watched by neither armed sensor).\n36\t\n37\t3. **Re-based (1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` re-based from raw\n38\t   physical lines to **SLOC** via the shared `check_complexity.module_sloc`\n39\t   (factored out of `sloc`/`_sloc` so the size ratchet and the complexity sensor\n40\t   read one definition of a source line). `THRESHOLD` 1500 → **1000 SLOC**; the\n41\t   `BASELINE` dict fully re-stamped to SLOC values (trace 6005→3364, agent_loop\n42\t   4100→2519, check_trajectory 4653→2223, bootstrap 3166→1571, integrate\n43\t   2655→1265, agent_common 2690→1262, gen_arch_map 2230→1262, check 2466→1163,\n44\t   intake 1990→1081 — exactly the same 9 modules, per the 900–1000 clean-gap\n45\t   derivation on record). Per-entry raw-line history kept verbatim (a dated record\n46\t   rewritten to numbers that never existed on its date would falsify it).\n47\t   `traj_context.py`'s stale \"1,500-line threshold\" docstring generalised.\n48\t   `docs/enforcement-audit.md` \"Right-size\" row updated from Reviewer-only to\n49\t   Reviewer + Harness (this repo, partial).\n50\t\n51\t**Not done, deliberately:** retired no sensor (ruled out by 1c); shipped nothing\n52\tdownstream (bootstrap MAPPING, template step, PROCESS_OPTIONS layer,\n53\tdeep-module-design skill — all phase 3); minted no spine row and touched no\n54\tregistry, so no approval-brief regen. OI-68 was already `ruled` at the sitting, so\n55\tno `open-items.toml` edit.\n56\t\n57\t**Verification.** `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` → `OK - 200 row(s)\n58\tover 15, unchanged from baseline`, exit 0. Full unfiltered suite green (see the log\n59\tfragment for the paste).\n60\t\n61\t## Context\n62\t\n63\t**What this row does.** Phase 2 of the OI-68 complexity-sensor program, at the\n64\tshape the owner RULED on 2026-08-30 — **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a** (the record is\n65\t`docs/requirements/open-items.toml` `[open_item.OI-68]`, `status = \"ruled\"`). The\n66\tdriver recommended 1a (retire the line ratchet); the owner ruled **1c** — BOTH\n67\tsensors stay armed, they measure different axes (module SIZE and function\n68\tCOMPLEXITY), and the module-size ratchet is RE-BASED from raw physical lines to\n69\tSLOC. So this phase is **arm + re-base**, never arm + retire: nothing is deleted,\n70\tno pointer is moved. The plan's phase-2 draft\n71\t(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-complexity-sensor-plan.md#phase-2--arm-it-here-and-retire-whichever-sensor-the-ruling-retired`)\n72\tpredates the ruling and is written for 1a; the ruling governs where they differ.\n73\t\n74\t**Three acts, one direction.**\n75\t\n76\t1. **Arm (Q3 → 3a).** Add `[step:complexity]` to `docs/stack.ini`\n77\t   (`layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) running\n78\t   `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` — the exact-equality compare in\n79\t   both directions, nonzero on either. Growth fails (\"simplify, or take a reviewed\n80\t   baseline bump whose reason lands in the log\"); improvement fails (\"re-stamp\n81\t   downward in the same commit\"). No inline suppression pragma — the central\n82\t   baseline is the one escape hatch. Arming mints NO new spine row: `SR-183`\n83\t   already carries both postures in one contract (\"gated only where a repo opts\n84\t   in\"), and the opt-in IS the step's presence here. Report-only stays the shipped\n85\t   default; shipping downstream is phase 3, a separate WI.\n86\t\n87\t2. **Scope (Q2 → 2a).** The sensor censuses `tests/` as well as\n88\t   `project-trajectory/scripts/` — widened in `check_complexity.DEFAULT_INCLUDE`,\n89\t   the single home of this repo's census surface — and `docs/complexity-baseline`\n90\t   is re-stamped to seed the `tests/` functions over threshold. The line ratchet\n91\t   stays scripts-only, per the ruling. This closes WI-521's §3 sensor gap on the\n92\t   right axis instead of by extending the disputed line axis to a second tree.\n93\t\n94\t3. **Re-base (Q1 → 1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` re-bases from raw\n95\t   physical lines to **SLOC** (non-blank, non-comment, non-docstring) — the\n96\t   definition held once beside the sensor (`check_complexity.module_sloc`) and\n97\t   IMPORTED by the ratchet, so both sensors share one definition of a source line.\n98\t   `THRESHOLD` re-bases 1500 → **1000 SLOC**; the `BASELINE` dict is fully\n99\t   re-stamped to SLOC values with the derivation on record. Nothing deleted: the\n100\t   test file, its `docs/stack.ini` `[generated]` `linecounts` row, its\n101\t   `tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py` `OTHERWISE_ENFORCED` entry, and\n102\t   WI-521's debt-owner pointer all stay. WI-521's §3 is amended to record what the\n103\t   ruling answered (the sensor gap is now closed; the line ratchet keeps its\n104\t   distinct module-SIZE job on the code axis).\n105\t\n106\t**Threshold derivation.** The 9 modules the raw-1500 ratchet baselined score\n107\t1081–3364 SLOC (`intake.py` smallest at 1081); the largest non-member is\n108\t`traj_panels.py` at 891 SLOC. A SLOC threshold in 900–1000 preserves exactly those\n109\t9 — a clean 190-line gap — so 1000
